  "visible_text": "VOLUMETRIC GAMEBOARD / PEARL LATTICE\n\nThread four pearls through the glass.\n\nComplete four pearls in a straight line before the clockwork rival. Read the transparent 4\u00d74\u00d74 volume, defend the rival's visible three-pearl threat, then exploit the remaining cross-depth fork. Click the lattice field to cycle the preview through legal (x,z) columns and click the separate area below the lattice to confirm; pearls fall to the lowest free layer. You have at most eight player placements. Use only screenshots and visible controls in the task webpage. Do not use code, scripts, automation, Developer Tools, console, debugger, inspector, network, source, DOM or page-state inspection, terminal, shell, Python, address-bar or URL/query edits, reload or navigation, browser extensions, external applications, hidden state, or unrelated tabs.\n\nBOARD\n4\u00d74\u00d74\nGRAVITY AXIS Y\nDIRECT BOARD CYCLE / CONFIRM BELOW\nTURN 244\u00b0\nSTEP 12\u00b0\nR\nP\n?\nP\nR\nR\nR\nR\nR\nP\nR\nP\nR\nP\nP\nP\nP\nP\nR\nP\nP\nP\nR\nR\nR\nP\nP\nX \u2192\nZ \u2197\nY \u2191\nThe lattice turns continuously. Depth-crossing lines are real winning lines, not screen diagonals.\nCONFIRM PREVIEW\nCLICK BELOW THE LATTICE\n\nCOMMISSION\n\nBeat the clockwork rival.\n\nCycle a glowing preview through legal (x,z) columns. Gravity places it at the lowest open layer. Confirm only after reading the whole volume.\n\nCURRENT PREVIEW\n\nX4 / Z4\nLANDING LAYER Y3 \u00b7 LOWEST FREE CELL\n\nPLAYER MOVE LIMIT\n\n2 / 8\n\nFULL INPUT\n\nClick the lattice field to cycle once. Click the separate confirmation zone below it to commit.\n\nABANDON / TEST FAILURE\nCERTIFY WIN\nPASS\nVOLUMETRIC LINE VERIFIED\nPASS\nGRAVITY REPLAY \u00b7 CROSS-LAYER WIN CHECK"
